From 165675950d18f1369d6ef671b90e1e94ba4ea016 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gabriel FORTE <2580288+g4bwy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 19:22:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 07/11] [Model Loader][Qwen4Exp] Serve PLE rows from checkpoint
 files via page cache (host_file_gather)

Adopt upstream PR #58815: --engram-config '{"host_file_gather": true}'
replaces the 47.6 GiB pinned-host PLE table with per-step host gathers
from the safetensors shard files - rows are preadv'd from page-cache
pages (FADV_WILLNEED coalesced ahead of each step, one dedup pass, one
pinned staging ring, one H2D copy), so the table's pages are reclaimable
by the kernel and never counted as worker RSS. Forward reads only the
fixed staging buffer; FULL CUDA graphs unaffected. Qwen4Exp only,
requires CUDA, wins over cpu_offload, rejected on ROCm/elastic-EP.
Motivating field data: PR #56273 ran the same checkpoint this way on a
128 GB DGX Spark (table on NVMe, FP8 rows, byte-exact over 1.02M staged
rows).

Upstream branch is 40 days old; drift adaptation in this port: the
module forward keeps #61454 sequence-parallel sharding with file-gather
as a third source beside prefetch and eager lookup; the loader keeps
the NVFP4 dtype guard beside the new accept_checkpoint_shard
interception; the base-class process_weights_after_loading binding
coexists with #61454's lookup_from_pinned/lookup_dtype; FileGather
learns the reduce_results kwarg and gains the finalize_prefetch ABC
stub; PR-era test call sites retargeted to the current signatures.

Verified on CPU box: test_ple + test_config failure set identical to
pristine base; engram config tests pass; the PR's file-gather unit
tests run green. Hardware on fender (2026-10-21/22): weight load 1:16
to 0:49, the table absent from worker RSS, needles exit 0, byte-exact
cold-table decode, decode-window acceptance 4.99 unchanged. Batch
prefill pays a per-step worker stream sync in staging (100/4 at
276-380 s against pinned's steady ~350; cold 1M +3 s); accepted trade
for 47.6 GB of pinned RAM and 27 s of boot. Pairs with the cache-drop
commit's PLE range-sparing under VLLM_SAFETENSORS_DROP_CACHE=1 to keep
the table page-cache resident.

Co-authored-by: Trosfy <61226342+Trosfy@users.noreply.github.com>
